                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/721: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-05T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                                1927—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>400. Your 1055, December 1, 6 p.m. Surtax appears contrary to Article 28 British
                    Treaty of 1858 and Article 7 Washington Conference Customs Treaty. As to protest
                    see Department’s 270, July 1, 1927.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
